{"q":"Unit test?","a":"Isolated automated check of small behavior."},{"q":"Assertion?","a":"Statement comparing expected and actual behavior."},{"q":"assertEqual?","a":"Checks values are equal."},{"q":"assertRaises?","a":"Checks an expected exception."},{"q":"unittest?","a":"Python standard-library test framework."},{"q":"Deterministic test?","a":"Same controlled input gives same result."},{"q":"Happy path?","a":"Expected successful behavior."},{"q":"Boundary test?","a":"Check at a limit or edge value."},{"q":"Regression test?","a":"Test preventing a known bug from returning."},{"q":"Traceback?","a":"Call path and exception details."},{"q":"Minimal reproduction?","a":"Smallest input that shows failure."},{"q":"Logging?","a":"Configurable diagnostic event recording."},{"q":"INFO level?","a":"Normal operational event."},{"q":"WARNING level?","a":"Unexpected but recoverable condition."},{"q":"ERROR level?","a":"Failed operation needing attention."},{"q":"breakpoint()?","a":"Pauses execution for debugging."},{"q":"Why avoid live APIs in unit tests?","a":"They are slow, costly, and nondeterministic."},{"q":"Why use temporary directories?","a":"Isolate filesystem tests."},{"q":"What should tests target?","a":"Observable behavior and contracts."},{"q":"Final test step?","a":"Run targeted and full relevant suite."}
